I just had a rather strange experience involving rings which I haven't
seen mentioned in previous posts.  I am playing version 3.0i
Patchlevel 7:

  I started as a wizard with a ring of teleport control and a ring of
shock resistance--both of which I wore from the begining.  On Level 2
I opened a booby-trapped chest and was jolted by a surge of
electricity.  I lost no hit points, but several of my goodies were
destroyed, including my ring of teleport control and a wand of
polymorph.  My ring of shock resistance seems to protect me, my body,
and itself from shocks (possibly not in that order) but not my hands
or my pack.  This was annoying, but perhaps understandable.
  The probable bug is what happened later.  On level three I was in a
shop and ate a tin of greasy jackel meat.  Being a slob, I got my
fingers greasy, and *all* my rings fell off--including the one which I
had verified was vaporized and no longer on my right hand.  I bought
back my ring of teleport control, and am now happy again.
   This experience has started me wondering about several things. Is
there any way I can get my wand back? (-: In the absence of this bug,
was I silly to put a more valuable ring on my right hand?  Does it
matter at all?  If so, how can I find out if my character is right
handed or left handed?


